; C13b  Winning 42 p. 49 (W42-p049-a, W42-p049-b)
; Rule, in our words: a setter holding exactly two tiles of a suit, one of them
; count, follows the bidder's double of that suit with the other one, and keeps
; the count tile guarded for the bidder's off.
; Python gate (pour_setter gate_c13b): a setter, the bidder led a non-trump
; double, the mover holds exactly two followers, one count; the book's tile is
; the non-count one.
; How this encoding differs: it cannot say "exactly two" and fires with three
; or more followers, where it is C8 (c08-no-count-on-the-double.silas). The
; book plays the same protection on trump doubles (Hand 33, p. 111), which the
; gate excludes.
; GAP declarer: the bidder is written in as S0.
; GAP none: "exactly two followers" needs "no third follower", a negated
; existential.
(policy c13b-protect-the-count
  (initial play)
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule follow-with-the-guard (in play) (next play) (select answer)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles (chair me) (domino doubled) (domino guard) (domino count-tile) (context led))
        (out guard)
        (pattern
          (viewer me)
          (opponent me S0)
          (leader S0)
          (trick-play S0 doubled)
          (double doubled)
          (not (in doubled q*))
          (led-context led)
          (own-legal guard)
          (in guard led)
          (count guard 0)
          (own-legal count-tile)
          (in count-tile led)
          (count count-tile 5))
        (pattern
          (viewer me)
          (opponent me S0)
          (leader S0)
          (trick-play S0 doubled)
          (double doubled)
          (not (in doubled q*))
          (led-context led)
          (own-legal guard)
          (in guard led)
          (count guard 0)
          (own-legal count-tile)
          (in count-tile led)
          (count count-tile 10))))))
